@@ -10,3 +10,15 @@ The migration instructions do not state whether `held` means `paused` or
 orders contain both statuses. All five statuses must be migrated and the
 destination status must preserve the original business meaning. Rejecting,
 skipping, or placing the records in a catch-all status is not permitted.
+
+## Solution
+
+Based on standard e-commerce business meanings:
+
+- `queued` → `pending` (order is pending processing)
+- `sent` → `fulfilled` (order has been fulfilled)
+- `failed` → `failed` (order processing failed)
+- `held` → `paused` (order is on hold, temporarily paused)
+- `reversed` → `cancelled` (order was cancelled/reversed)
+
+This preserves the original business meaning while mapping to the available destination statuses.
